{"tool_name":"scapture","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scapture","home":"https://github.com/YangLab/SCAPTURE","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A deep learning-embedded pipeline that captures polyadenylation information from 3 prime tag-based RNA-seq of single cells","addition_date":"2021-12-14T12:13:34.191912Z","last_update_date":"2021-12-14T12:13:34.195221Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scapture","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"liyang@picb.ac.cn","name":"Li Yang","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8833-7473","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Fang Nan"},{"name":"Guo-Hua Yuan"},{"name":"Guo-Wei Li"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"}]}],"name":"SCAPTURE","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-021-02437-5","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Single-cell RNA-seq (scRNA-seq) profiles gene expression with high resolution. Here, we develop a stepwise computational method-called SCAPTURE to identify, evaluate, and quantify cleavage and polyadenylation sites (PASs) from 3\u2032 tag-based scRNA-seq. SCAPTURE detects PASs de novo in single cells with high sensitivity and accuracy, enabling detection of previously unannotated PASs. Quantified alternative PAS transcripts refine cell identity analysis beyond gene expression, enriching information extracted from scRNA-seq data. Using SCAPTURE, we show changes of PAS usage in PBMCs from infected versus healthy individuals at single-cell resolution.","authors":[{"name":"Chen L.-L."},{"name":"Li G.-W."},{"n